  "note": "Run on the live AwwO, in the operator’s own account and workspace, on 2026-10-26, every agent on Claude Opus 5.5 working in its own sandbox computer. The film answers an Opus 5.5 video prompt by Ryven (x.com/imryven/status/2105719735438495965, prompt 11798 of YouMind’s Opus 5.5 collection): a multi-agent coding setup shown as a live terminal dashboard. AwwO’s version is a live dashboard of one real canvas run, the published record of the homepage case Umber, and states only facts from that record. The canvas’s text was written for this film by the operator beforehand: the Director’s task (the prompt adapted to AwwO, with the facts the film may state and the look), the kernel contract every module writes to, each builder’s duty, and the tester’s and the editor’s tasks. What is seen and heard is what the canvas’s agents wrote. The canvas ran three times, each run after the first running only the nodes it named, on the kept outputs of the rest. The first (09:30 to 09:51 UTC) finished everything but the edit: the render worker then live could not yet record a page’s sound, so the edit refused the timeline’s music (the worker took page sounds from 09:51 UTC). The second (10:03 to 10:06) ran the edit again, which delivered a film, but its closing mark was not AwwO’s Fold mark: the mark’s paths were in the Director’s task, which its brief did not repeat, so Header and counters, the module that draws it, drew a mark of its own. The third (12:18 to 12:44) ran Header and counters again with the mark’s paths in its own task, then the assembly, the tester (whose task now also times the frames with the page’s timers stopped, as AwwO’s renderer does), the editor and the edit: the film here. The tester found 13 of the page’s 13 tests passing and all 4 planted failures caught, and fixed nothing; the editor kept the film as one piece of 20 s; and the edit node rendered it from the page and recorded the page’s own sound (window.renderAudio), with no model. The canvas’s Review node ran beside the edit and is not part of this case.",
